        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-04T17:30:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can\u0027t we do this automatically at [1]? We want to update the sync id every time we emit a barrier for that buffer.",
      "revId": "8f46df7b7e60836940138121fc9f87dfc259eedb",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "757fc01b_71cabdeb",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/BufferVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 407,
      "author": {
        "id": 3461520
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-05T13:58:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We want to update the sync Id every time we have a bound buffer that is possibly mutated by the operation ( usually the dispatch). We might need a fence for a buffer that end up being read-only forever in the future requiring no new barrier.",
      "parentUuid": "29586e90_106dfcdf",
      "revId": "8f46df7b7e60836940138121fc9f87dfc259eedb",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ddf6ab40_38362f44",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/BufferVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 407,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-05T14:06:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can use `readOnly` to know if the buffer might be mutated or not in that function.",
      "parentUuid": "757fc01b_71cabdeb",
      "revId": "8f46df7b7e60836940138121fc9f87dfc259eedb",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5f796ce_b5b47373",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/BufferVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 407,
      "author": {
        "id": 3461520
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-05T14:10:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is that we need to Sync (Fence) after the we add the barrier. We cannot do it at that location because we dont know until the end if we are adding in the barrier.  \n\nI though of having a list of buffers that would then need updating but I dont like the idea of storing (even temporarily) a list of unowned buffer pointers.",
      "parentUuid": "ddf6ab40_38362f44",
      "revId": "8f46df7b7e60836940138121fc9f87dfc259eedb",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
